  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Doxepin is a tricyclic antidepressant used to treat depression, and as a topical antipruritic to relieve itching of the skin. It remains an approved medicine and is used fairly widely, available both as an oral antidepressant and as a skin cream.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q71704041&quot;>Wikidata Q71704041</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>doxepin</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>D04AX01, N06AA12</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB01142&quot;>DB01142</a></td></tr><tr><td>PubChem CID:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/667468&quot;>667468</a></td></tr><tr><td>ChEBI:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:4710&quot;>4710</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q71704041&quot;>Q71704041</a></td></tr><tr><td>formula:</td><td>C19H21NO</td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>279.383 g/mol (PubChem)</td></tr></table></body></html>"));
